Z||000000||jerpro||05-06-2001||06:56 PM||||My dad is planning on changing his hard drive on his laptop and although I have dealt with computer hardware for many years I have never touched a laptop and am scared I am going to break it or something.<BR>If anyone knows how to open one or can give me a couple pointers I would appreciate it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DISenchanted||05-06-2001||07:36 PM||||What make and model of laptop?  I've taken apart quite a few and would be more then happy to help.<P>DISenchnated||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||05-06-2001||08:06 PM||||Usually, changing the hard disk of a laptop is one of the easier things to do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Be aware though that you need a special HD, probably one that is made for the laptop.<P>On most laptops, the HD can be accessed trough the bottom of the laptop. Turn the thing over and look for a small cover with a few screws. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||05-06-2001||10:41 PM||||I think all you do is push a button, flip the cover, and type away.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||beer_stud_21||05-07-2001||02:46 PM||||BFH is a sure bet.  But if you go this route, there is usually lots of little pieces left over that you can never figure out where they went.  hehe.  As for the hard drive, they need to be quite a bit smaller than a normal hard drive you would put in your standard PC, but they are not specific to the exact laptop.  If you get the bottom of the case off you will probably see the HD, its about the bigest thing in there.  Just be sure you use a grounding strap so you don't accidently zap something.  Better safe than sorry.  If you don't have a grounding strap the next best thing is to do it in your kitchen, just make sure your butt-naked so you wont build up static electricity.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I opened up a Powerbook G4 the other day to install ram.  It's a bit scary playin around in a $2600.00 computer, but if your grounded, and carefull I don't think you have much chance of seriously hurting anything. Just put everything back the way you found it and it should work fine.<P>-Marlin ||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||05-07-2001||06:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beer_stud_21:<BR><B>If you don't have a grounding strap the next best thing is to do <I>IT</I> in your kitchen, just make sure your butt-naked so you wont build up static electricity.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>That's a funny statment when it's taken out of the whole text.LOL<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DISenchanted||05-07-2001||08:27 PM||||Hey Beer Stud,  is that your Powerbook?  I have one, and I love mine.  Installing ram in a PBG4 doesn't count as taking it apart.  Lift 2 tabs and you're in.<P>DISenchanted||||reg||1
Z||000007||beer_stud_21||05-08-2001||02:46 PM||||OMG... LOL!  good one 2x...  But who has to wear the grounding strap?  And wouldn't it be pretty easy to get all tied up..  (Now there's one for ya.. hehe)<P>As for the TiBook.  No, its not mine, I was setting it up for my uncle who took it to Rome to work.  The bastard!  I loved that thing.  I'm going to wait till I go back to school next simester then get a new iBook- they are more in my price range.  And, ya- its pretty damn easy to add ram, I had it done in about 5 minutes.  I didn't even use a grounding strap!  Fully clothed minus socks no less.  But i'm in hawaii where we get like 300 inches of rain a year. There isn't much static electricity here.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000008||KRMFiero||05-08-2001||02:52 PM||||Pretty much every laptop I have ever seen the HD comes out through the keyboard (keyboard comes out, another was is some slide out through the front or side.....  we will neeed to know what kind of laptop...easyer way would be to go to the manurfactures website and download the users guide thing<P>Kyle||||reg||1
